  "locked": false,
  "title": "Adoption agency: invoke custom element reactions once the algorithm finishes",
  "user": {
    "login": "noamr",
    "id": 88566,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTY2",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88566?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/noamr",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/noamr/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "The adoption agency algorithm removes and inserts nodes directly without an element queue on the custom element reactions stack. During normal parsing (when the JavaScript execution context stack is empty), `disconnectedCallback` and `connectedCallback` reactions from reparenting the furthest block and its children are enqueued on the backup element queue and only run at the next microtask checkpoint (such as at a following `</script>` end tag, after any intervening tokens—or the new element for an `<a>` or `<nobr>` start tag—have already been parsed). When the parser is driven from script (e.g., via `document.write()`), `document.write()`'s `[CEReactions]` extended attribute makes its element queue the current element queue, so those reactions are enqueued there and only run when `document.write()` returns, after a following `<script>` has already executed.\n\nPush a new element queue before running the inner adoption agency algorithm and pop and invoke it once the algorithm finishes, matching how \"insert an element at the adjusted insertion location\" handles reactions.\n\nWrapping the algorithm as a whole rather than each DOM operation inside it ensures that:\n\n- No custom element callback reactions caused by the algorithm's tree mutations run while the tree is in an intermediate state of the algorithm (for example, while a node has been moved into a clone created by the inner loop that has not yet been inserted into the common ancestor).\n- Each custom element's callbacks observe the final tree produced by the algorithm, grouped per element in the order the elements were first enqueued.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64911.\n\nFixes #13072.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (TBD)\n   * Gecko (TBD)\n   * WebKit (TBD)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64911\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: TBD\n   * Gecko: TBD\n   * WebKit: TBD\n   * Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): N/A\n   * Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): N/A\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13215/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 11:20 AM UTC (1c0d36b)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13215/2f98c06...1c0d36b/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 11:20 AM UTC (1c0d36b)\">diff</a> )",
